  {
    "id": "paper:867752822639165809::conclusion_1",
    "global_id": "gcn_9ec8db18b26049e8",
    "order": 1,
    "title": "Empirical characterization: three-stage training dynamics of out-of-distribution metrics",
    "content": "The trajectory of out-of-distribution (OOD) detection performance, measured by the area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (AUROC) and related metrics, during supervised training decomposes into three distinct stages: (A) an initial stage where training and test error fall and AUROC improves; (B) a subsequent overfitting stage where the training error approaches zero and test error can continue to decrease while AUROC decreases (i.e., OOD performance degrades as the model memorizes and learns redundant features); and (C) a final instability stage where classification test error is stable but AUROC (and other OOD metrics) varies sharply across nearby checkpoints, making final-checkpoint selection unreliable.",
    "labeled_segments": {
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "The trajectory of out-of-distribution (OOD) detection performance, ",
          "label": "assertion [1]"
        },
        {
          "text": "measured by the area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (AUROC) and related metrics, ",
          "label": "elaboration"
        },
        {
          "text": "during supervised training decomposes into three distinct stages: (A) an initial stage where training and test error fall and AUROC improves; (B) a subsequent overfitting stage where the training error approaches zero and test error can continue to decrease while AUROC decreases ",
          "label": "assertion [1]"
        },
        {
          "text": "(i.e., OOD performance degrades as the model memorizes and learns redundant features); ",
          "label": "elaboration"
        },
        {
          "text": "and (C) a final instability stage where classification test error is stable but AUROC (and other OOD metrics) varies sharply across nearby checkpoints, making final-checkpoint selection unreliable.",
