    "title": "Linear-Gaussian risk formulas and LASSO solution: analytic link between common features, in-distribution accuracy and out-of-distribution risk",
    "content": "For a simplified linear-Gaussian model that isolates a special discriminative feature and \\(d\\) abundant weak common features, the Bayes classifier and its in-distribution (ID) classification risk and out-of-distribution (OOD) detection (rejection) risk admit closed-form expressions: let ID feature vectors \\(\\boldsymbol{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d+1}\\) be drawn as \\(\\boldsymbol{x} \\sim \\mathcal{N}(y \\cdot \\boldsymbol{\\mu}_\\text{ID}, \\sigma^2 \\boldsymbol{I})\\) with \\(y\\stackrel{u.a.r.}{\\sim}\\{-1,+1\\}\\) and \\(\\boldsymbol{\\mu}_\\text{ID}=(1,\\eta,\\dots,\\eta)\\), and OOD feature vectors be drawn as \\(\\boldsymbol{x} \\sim \\mathcal{N}(q \\cdot \\boldsymbol{\\mu}_\\text{OOD}, \\sigma^2 \\boldsymbol{I})\\) with \\(q\\stackrel{u.a.r.}{\\sim}\\{-1,+1\\}\\) and \\(\\boldsymbol{\\mu}_\\text{OOD}=(0,\\eta,\\dots,\\eta)\\), with isotropic noise variance \\(\\sigma^2\\). The Bayes logit is\n      \\[\n      f_{\\mathrm{Bayes}}(\\boldsymbol{x}) = x_1 + \\eta\\sum_{i=2}^{d+1} x_i,\n      \\]\n      and the resulting risks simplify to\n      \\[\n      \\mathcal{R}_{\\mathrm{ID}}(f_{\\mathrm{Bayes}})=\\Pr\\!\\left\\{\\mathcal{N}(0,1)>\\frac{\\sqrt{1+d\\eta^2}}{\\sigma}\\right\\},\n      \\]\n      \\[\n      \\mathcal{R}_{\\mathrm{OOD}}(f_{\\mathrm{Bayes}})=\\Pr\\!\\left\\{\\mathcal{N}(0,1)>\\frac{\\delta-d\\eta^2}{\\sigma\\sqrt{1+d\\eta^2}}\\right\\}+\\Pr\\!\\left\\{\\mathcal{N}(0,1)>\\frac{\\delta+d\\eta^2}{\\sigma\\sqrt{1+d\\eta^2}}\\right\\},\n      \\]\n      where \\(\\delta\\) is the rejection threshold. These formulas show that increasing the number \\(d\\) of common weak features (with \\(0<\\eta\\ll1\\) and \\(d\\gg1\\)) can markedly increase OOD risk while only slowly improving ID classification. Further, solving the squared-error empirical risk with least absolute shrinkage and selection operator (LASSO) regularization parameter \\(\\lambda\\),\n      \\[\n      \\min_{\\boldsymbol{w}}\\ \\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\\sim\\mathcal{D}_\\text{ID}}\\!\\left\\{\\tfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{\\boldsymbol{w}^\\top\\boldsymbol{x}}{\\sigma}-y\\right)^2+\\lambda\\|\\boldsymbol{w}\\|_1\\right\\},\n      \\]\n      yields the closed-form trimmed coefficient vector\n      \\[\n      f_{\\text{LASSO}}(\\boldsymbol{x}) = (1-\\lambda)_+\\,x_1 + \\sum_{i=2}^{d+1} (\\eta-\\lambda)_+\\, x_i,\n      \\]\n      where \\((\\cdot)_+\\) denotes the positive part. This analytic solution demonstrates that an \\(L_1\\) penalty (feature selection) can suppress coefficients on abundant weak common features (by choosing \\(\\lambda\\approx\\eta\\)), thereby reducing OOD detection risk at controlled cost to ID accuracy.",
